            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0441" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 250.</note>
                <head>Mr. Thornton to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 2, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In reply to your note of yesterday’s date,
                    I have the honor to inform you that although I am aware of the announcement
                    recently made by the Canadian government of their intention to issue no more
                    licenses to foreign fishermen, I have received no official information to that
                    effect from the Governor General of Canada.</p>
                <p>Nor am I aware of the existence of any recent law or regulations which may have
                    been issued upon the subject of the fisheries. I will, however, without delay,
                    make inquiries upon the subject from the Governor General, and will have the
                    honor of communicating to you the result.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWARD THORNTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
